{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966783,"nonce":"htPWusQ8KnG8Ch2HMIXMpF0Etdc=","title":"Incremental subtree rebuild (rebuild_children_in_place) applied inline + #id styles but NOT","message":"When a `Stateful` rebuilds a changed child subtree (e.g. toggling an accordion item), the freshly-built nodes kept their inline + `#id` styles but lost every `.class`-driven property. Most visible for LAYOUT props (padding / size / flex), which are never otherwise re-derived: the just-toggled accordion trigger collapsed to zero padding + height while untouched siblings kept theirs; a hovered menubar submenu row shifted. Symptom fingerprint: **only the most-recently-rebuilt node malforms; toggling another fixes the first and breaks the new one.**\n\n**Root cause.** `collect_render_props` / `collect_render_props_boxed` apply inline + `#id` styles only (they DO register the new nodes' classes, but don't apply class rules). Class rules are applied by the separate stylesheet passes — `apply_stylesheet_base_styles_for_subtree` (visual: bg/color) and `apply_stylesheet_layout_overrides` (taffy: padding/size/flex). The incremental rebuild path `rebuild_children_in_place` (renderer/build/diff.rs — the path `rebuild_changed_subtrees` uses, which most statefuls hit) called neither. The routed / full-replace paths in subtree.rs called base-for-subtree but there was no layout-for-subtree variant at all.\n\n**Fix (blinc_layout).** Added `apply_stylesheet_layout_overrides_for_subtree` (a subtree-filtered variant of the whole-tree layout pass; `collect_subtree_ids` widened to `pub(crate)`), and call it plus `apply_stylesheet_base_styles_for_subtree(parent, None)` at the end of `rebuild_children_in_place` and the three routed/full-replace sites. Class-registration during collect means the class index matches the fresh nodes, so the passes find them. Commit `31d407f2`.\n\n**Also:** a class-only widget with NO builder fallback is doubly exposed — it also breaks on the INITIAL render if the node is built after the whole-tree pass (a default-open accordion item). The cn convention (see cn_styles.rs's `.cn-menubar-item` note) is that every menu primitive carries a builder `.py/.px` fallback EQUAL to its CSS `padding`; the accordion trigger omitted it. Add the matched fallback (`py(4)/px(3)` == `space-4 / space-3`) — no shift when the class applies, robust when it doesn't. This is the same pattern as the menubar fix in `74712e6a`.\n\nExplains and largely resolves the class-drop half of project css overrides consistency. Related bake-time class issue: gotcha foreground breaks composite promotion.","files":null}]}